       28.9  (bw   4.92 GiB/s, md   169.5 kIOPS)  + the LD_PRELOAD interception library in every rank (no FUSE channel, no kernel on the I/O path; implemented: io500_run.py --client auto probes it against FUSE and uses the faster; a no-op on a run that already used it)
       28.9  (bw   4.92 GiB/s, md   169.5 kIOPS)  + one-sided reads and lookups (client RDMA READs stripes and MDT entries; implemented: io500_run.py --direct-read auto probes it; a no-op on a run that already used it -- its effect is in the measured per-op server CPU)
       28.9  (bw   4.92 GiB/s, md   169.5 kIOPS)  + the OST's NVMe tier for the 300 s write phases (implemented: roce/native/ost_tier.c, io500_run.py --ost-tier auto; a no-op on a run that already had it -- its limits are then the drives' capacity and write bandwidth)
